---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Donkey Nobody Redeemed — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 10"
  description="Bekhorot 10: a firstborn donkey's whole life, judged by Rabbi Yehuda and two readings of Rabbi Shimon. Sort carcasses between village and market, scrub the donkey's timeline from birth to the cleaver, and balance the scale that decides whether a woman is betrothed with it."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#1d1a17] !text-[#efe8da]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#d8b25a]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 10, 28 September 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">The Donkey Nobody Redeemed</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#d8b25a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">וְאִם לֹא תִפְדֶּה וַעֲרַפְתּוֹ</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
          A firstborn donkey is holy until its owner hands a kohen a lamb. If he won't, the Torah says to break
          its neck (Exodus 13:13). Today's daf asks what you may do with that donkey, alive and dead, and what it
          takes for meat nobody plans to eat to count as food.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 70" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <line x1="10" y1="52" x2="590" y2="52" stroke="#4a4235" stroke-width="2" />
          <g id="hero-donkey" fill="#8c8a86">
            <ellipse cx="80" cy="34" rx="26" ry="12" />
            <rect x="60" y="40" width="5" height="12" /><rect x="94" y="40" width="5" height="12" />
            <path d="M103 28 L118 14 L126 18 L112 34 Z" />
            <path d="M118 14 L116 3 L121 12 Z M122 15 L124 4 L126 14 Z" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#efe8da">
            <ellipse cx="520" cy="38" rx="17" ry="10" />
            <circle cx="538" cy="32" r="6" />
            <rect x="508" y="44" width="3" height="8" fill="#a39a8a" /><rect x="528" y="44" width="3" height="8" fill="#a39a8a" />
          </g>
          <circle cx="300" cy="40" r="9" fill="#d8b25a" /><text x="300" y="44" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#1d1a17">₪</text>
          <text x="300" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#a39a8a">a lamb for the kohen?</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#3a342b] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">Village or market</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
          Meat only picks up food impurity if it counts as food. If people nearby would normally eat it, it
          already does. If not, someone has to <em>intend</em> to eat it (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">מַחְשָׁבָה</span>).
          The mishna in <a class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#d8b25a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Oktzin.3.3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Okatzin 3:3</a>
          sorts carcasses by where they're found: in the villages, where gentiles are pickier, or in the big
          market towns, where someone eats almost anything. Each carcass lands on the map. Rule it.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="zone rounded-lg border border-[#3a342b] p-3" id="zone-village">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 40" class="h-10 w-full"><path d="M10 35 L10 22 L22 12 L34 22 L34 35 Z M46 35 L46 25 L55 17 L64 25 L64 35 Z M80 35 L80 20 L94 9 L108 20 L108 35 Z" fill="none" stroke="#7fa88a" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            <p class="text-center text-sm !text-[#7fa88a]">Villages <span dir="rtl" lang="he">כְּפָרִים</span></p>
            <div id="drop-village" class="mt-2 min-h-[2.5rem] text-center text-3xl"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="zone rounded-lg border border-[#3a342b] p-3" id="zone-market">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 120 40" class="h-10 w-full"><path d="M8 35 L8 16 L112 16 L112 35 M8 16 L20 6 L100 6 L112 16 M30 16 L30 35 M60 16 L60 35 M90 16 L90 35" fill="none" stroke="#d8b25a" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
            <p class="text-center text-sm !text-[#d8b25a]">Markets <span dir="rtl" lang="he">שְׁוָקִים</span></p>
            <div id="drop-market" class="mt-2 min-h-[2.5rem] text-center text-3xl"></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="sort-card" class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-[#26221d] p-4">
          <p class="text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]"><span id="sort-count"></span></p>
          <p id="sort-q" class="mt-1 text-xl font-bold"></p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <button class="act" data-v="food">Already food</button>
            <button class="act" data-v="intent">Needs someone's intent</button>
          </div>
          <p id="sort-fb" class="mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <button id="sort-next" class="act mt-3 hidden">Next carcass</button>
        </div>

        <div id="contra" class="mt-6 hidden">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Test a theory: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">אִיסּוּרוֹ חִישּׁוּבוֹ</span></h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
            The Sages before Rav Sheshet proposed that a food's prohibition counts as its intent: because a Jew
            is forbidden to eat it, it's significant enough to be food automatically
            (<a class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#d8b25a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.10a.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener">10a:6</a>).
            Every carcass above is forbidden to a Jew. Tap every ruling the theory can't explain, then check.
          </p>
          <div id="contra-grid" class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2"></div>
          <button id="contra-check" class="act mt-3">Check</button>
          <div id="contra-fb" class="mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>

        <div id="crow" class="mt-6 hidden rounded-lg border border-[#3a342b] p-4">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold">The practice crow</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
            Nimos, brother of Rabbi Yehoshua HaGarsi, told Rabbi Yosei that if someone slaughters a crow to
            practice slaughtering, its blood still makes food susceptible to impurity. Rabbi Eliezer says the
            blood of slaughter always does
            (<a class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#d8b25a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.10b.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">10b:2</a>).
            They seem to say the same thing, so what do they actually disagree about? The Gemara gives two readings.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex gap-2" role="tablist">
            <button class="pill" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-crow="0">First reading</button>
            <button class="pill" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-crow="1">Second reading</button>
          </div>
          <p id="crow-text" class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed"></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II ============ -->
      <section id="part2" class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a342b] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">A donkey's life, three ways</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
          Rabbi Yehuda forbids any benefit from an unredeemed firstborn donkey. Rabbi Shimon permits it. What
          happens after the neck is broken splits the amoraim: Rabba, Rav Naḥman in the name of Rabba bar Avuh,
          and Reish Lakish say Rabbi Shimon concedes it's forbidden then. Rabbi Yoḥanan (some say Rabbi Elazar)
          says he still permits it. Drag the timeline to each stop and rule for all three.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-[#26221d] p-4">
          <svg id="life-svg" viewBox="0 0 320 110" class="w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="life-cap"></svg>
          <label for="life" class="sr-only">Stop on the donkey's timeline</label>
          <input id="life" type="range" min="0" max="3" step="1" value="0" class="mt-2 w-full accent-[#d8b25a]" />
          <div class="mt-1 grid grid-cols-4 text-center text-xs !text-[#a39a8a]" aria-hidden="true">
            <span>Alive: value</span><span>Alive: its body</span><span>Redeemed</span><span>Neck broken</span>
          </div>
          <p id="life-cap" class="mt-4 text-lg font-bold"></p>
          <p id="life-sub" class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]"></p>

          <div id="tools" class="mt-3 hidden">
            <p class="text-base !text-[#cfc5b2]">The owner refused to redeem it. Which of these may he use?</p>
            <div id="tool-rack" class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2"></div>
            <p id="tool-fb" class="mt-2 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></p>
          </div>

          <div id="lenses" class="mt-4 grid gap-2"></div>
          <button id="life-check" class="act mt-3">Lock in this stop</button>
          <p id="life-fb" class="mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>

        <div id="proofs" class="mt-6 hidden">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Rav Naḥman's two proofs</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
            Rav Naḥman argues each baraita below only makes sense as Rabbi Shimon's, which would mean Rabbi Shimon
            forbids the dead donkey. Could Rabbi Yehuda be the tanna anyway?
          </p>
          <div id="proof-list" class="mt-3 grid gap-3"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III ============ -->
      <section id="part3" class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a342b] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">The betrothal scale</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
          The mishna in <a class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#d8b25a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin.56b" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kiddushin 56b</a>
          says a man who betroths a woman with a firstborn donkey hasn't betrothed her. Whose view is that? Under
          Rabbi Shimon she'd get the donkey's whole value. Under Rabbi Yehuda she'd get what's left after the
          lamb: the donkey's value once redeemed, minus the lamb. Rav finds a case where that's zero. Find it too.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-5 rounded-lg bg-[#26221d] p-4">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Whose view">
            <button class="pill" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-lens="rs">Rabbi Shimon</button>
            <button class="pill" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-lens="ry-any">Rabbi Yehuda, lamb of any value</button>
            <button class="pill" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-lens="ry-shekel">Rabbi Yehuda, lamb at least a shekel</button>
          </div>
          <svg id="scale" viewBox="0 0 320 170" class="mt-4 w-full" role="img" aria-labelledby="scale-read"></svg>
          <label for="donkey-val" class="mt-2 block text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]">Donkey's value: <span id="donkey-val-out" class="font-bold !text-[#efe8da]"></span></label>
          <input id="donkey-val" type="range" min="1" max="16" step="1" value="8" class="w-full accent-[#d8b25a]" />
          <p id="scale-read" class="mt-3 text-lg" aria-live="polite"></p>
          <p id="scale-win" class="mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed"></p>
        </div>

        <div id="verse" class="mt-6 hidden">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Where does the shekel come from?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
            A baraita reads the doubled <span dir="rtl" lang="he">״תִּפְדֶּה״</span> as "redeem it right away, redeem
            it with anything." That rules out comparing the donkey to a firstborn son, redeemed after thirty days
            with five shekels. But then Rabbi Yosei bar Yehuda's shekel minimum is stuck: if the comparison holds,
            he should need five; if it doesn't, why one? Which verse gives him the shekel?
          </p>
          <div id="verse-choices" class="mt-3 grid gap-2"></div>
          <p id="verse-fb" class="mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div id="finale" class="mt-12 hidden rounded-lg border border-[#d8b25a]/40 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-3xl font-bold !text-[#d8b25a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">הֲדַרַן עֲלָךְ</p>
        <p id="finale-text" class="mt-2 text-base !text-[#cfc5b2]"></p>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-14 border-t border-[#3a342b] pt-8">
        <h3 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#d8b25a]">Learn the real daf</h3>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed !text-[#cfc5b2]">
          Bekhorot 10 finishes Rabbi Shimon's list of forbidden-for-benefit foods that can still become impure
          (meat cooked in milk, since it once was permitted) and tests Rava's claim that nobody holds "its
          prohibition is its intent." It then goes through the firstborn donkey's legal life: the baraita of the
          cleaver and the forbidden killing methods, Rav Naḥman's two proofs, and the Kiddushin mishna. It ends
          with the doubled <em>tifdeh</em> and Rava's shekel of the Sanctuary.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.10a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#d8b25a]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#d8b25a] hover:border-[#d8b25a]">Bekhorot 10 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.10a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a342b] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a8a] hover:border-[#d8b25a]">Rashi ×49 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.10a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a342b] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a8a] hover:border-[#d8b25a]">Steinsaltz ×45 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.10a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a342b] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a8a] hover:border-[#d8b25a]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×41 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.10a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a342b] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a8a] hover:border-[#d8b25a]">Tosafot ×8 ↗</a>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#3a342b] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a39a8a]">Rashash ×8</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#7a7264]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#a39a8a]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .act {
      border-radius: 0.35rem;
      border: 1px solid #5a5143;
      background: #1d1a17;
      color: #efe8da;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s;
    }
    .act:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #d8b25a; }
    .act:focus-visible, .pill:focus-visible, .cell:focus-visible, input[type='range']:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #d8b25a; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .act:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: default; }
    .act.ok { border-color: #7fa88a; background: #1f2a22; color: #cfe6d4 !important; }
    .act.bad { border-color: #b4553a; background: #2c1b15; color: #f0c2b2 !important; }
    .pill {
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid #5a5143;
      color: #cfc5b2;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .pill[aria-selected='true'], .pill[aria-checked='true'] { background: #d8b25a; border-color: #d8b25a; color: #1d1a17 !important; }
    .cell {
      text-align: left;
      border-radius: 0.35rem;
      border: 1px solid #3a342b;
      background: #1d1a17;
      padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: #efe8da;
    }
    .cell[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: #d8b25a; background: #2e281c; }
    .cell.ok { border-color: #7fa88a !important; }
    .cell.bad { border-color: #b4553a !important; }
    .lens-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center; }
    .verdict { min-width: 7.5rem; }
    .verdict[data-v='P'] { border-color: #7fa88a; color: #cfe6d4 !important; }
    .verdict[data-v='F'] { border-color: #b4553a; color: #f0c2b2 !important; }
    .drop-in { animation: dropin 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.3, 1.4, 0.6, 1); display: inline-block; }
    #beam { transition: transform 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.3, 1.3, 0.6, 1); }
    @keyframes dropin { from { transform: translateY(-30px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .drop-in { animation: none !important; }
      #beam { transition: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#d8b25a] underline decoration-[#4a4235] hover:!text-[#f0d68a]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const score: Record<string, number | undefined> = { sort: undefined, contra: undefined, life: undefined, proofs: undefined, scale: undefined, verse: undefined };
    const MAX = { sort: 8, contra: 1, life: 12, proofs: 2, scale: 1, verse: 1 };

    // =============== PART I: village or market ===============
    type Carcass = { id: string; emoji: string; name: string; where: 'village' | 'market'; ans: 'food' | 'intent'; why: string; ref: string };
    const CARCASSES: Carcass[] = [
      { id: 'horse-v', emoji: '🐴', name: 'A dead horse (a non-kosher animal)', where: 'village', ans: 'intent', why: 'A non-kosher animal\'s carcass needs intent anywhere. Almost nobody eats horse.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:9' },
      { id: 'cow-v', emoji: '🐄', name: 'An unslaughtered kosher cow (nevela)', where: 'village', ans: 'food', why: 'A kosher animal\'s carcass is food anywhere: gentiles eat it, so no intent is needed.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:10' },
      { id: 'bird-v', emoji: '🕊️', name: 'An unslaughtered kosher bird', where: 'village', ans: 'intent', why: 'In the villages people don\'t usually eat a bird that died on its own, so it needs intent.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:9' },
      { id: 'bird-m', emoji: '🕊️', name: 'The same kosher bird', where: 'market', ans: 'food', why: 'In the market towns someone eats it, so it\'s food already.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:10' },
      { id: 'fat-v', emoji: '🧈', name: 'Forbidden fat (ḥelev) of a kosher animal', where: 'village', ans: 'intent', why: 'Ḥelev in the villages needs intent.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:9' },
      { id: 'fat-m', emoji: '🧈', name: 'The same ḥelev', where: 'market', ans: 'food', why: 'Ḥelev in the markets is food already.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:10' },
      { id: 'horse-m', emoji: '🐴', name: 'A dead horse', where: 'market', ans: 'intent', why: '"In any place": even the market doesn\'t make a non-kosher animal\'s carcass into food.', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:9' },
      { id: 'pig-m', emoji: '🐖', name: 'A pig carcass, according to Rabbi Shimon', where: 'market', ans: 'food', why: 'Rabbi Shimon: camel, hare, hyrax and pig need no intent at all, because each has <em>some</em> kosher sign (cud or split hooves).', ref: 'Bekhorot 10a:11' },
    ];
    let sortIdx = 0;
    let sortRight = 0;
    const answered: Record<string, boolean> = {};
    function renderSort() {
      const c = CARCASSES[sortIdx];
      $('sort-count').textContent = `Carcass ${sortIdx + 1} of ${CARCASSES.length}, found in the ${c.where === 'village' ? 'villages' : 'markets'}`;
      $('sort-q').textContent = `${c.emoji} ${c.name}`;
      const drop = $(c.where === 'village' ? 'drop-village' : 'drop-market');
      const s = document.createElement('span');
      s.className = 'drop-in';
      s.textContent = c.emoji;
      s.title = c.name;
      drop.appendChild(s);
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#sort-card .act[data-v]').forEach((b) => {
        b.disabled = false;
        b.classList.remove('ok', 'bad');
      });
      $('sort-fb').classList.add('hidden');
      $('sort-next').classList.add('hidden');
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#sort-card .act[data-v]').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const c = CARCASSES[sortIdx];
        const ok = b.dataset.v === c.ans;
        if (ok) sortRight++;
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#sort-card .act[data-v]').forEach((x) => {
          x.disabled = true;
          if (x.dataset.v === c.ans) x.classList.add('ok');
        });
        if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad');
        const fb = $('sort-fb');
        fb.classList.remove('hidden');
        fb.innerHTML = `<strong class="${ok ? '!text-[#7fa88a]' : '!text-[#e0876a]'}">${ok ? 'Right.' : 'Not quite.'}</strong> ${c.why} ${link(c.ref)}`;
        const next = $('sort-next');
        next.classList.remove('hidden');
        next.textContent = sortIdx === CARCASSES.length - 1 ? 'Test a theory' : 'Next carcass';
        next.focus();
      }),
    );
    $('sort-next').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (sortIdx < CARCASSES.length - 1) {
        sortIdx++;
        renderSort();
        return;
      }
      score.sort = sortRight;
      $('sort-card').innerHTML = `<p class="text-base">${sortRight}/8 carcasses ruled right. None of them needs contact with liquid (<em>hekhsher</em>) either: a carcass is impure in its own right.</p>`;
      $('contra').classList.remove('hidden');
      renderContra();
      $('contra').scrollIntoView({ behavior: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'start' });
    });

    function renderContra() {
      const g = $('contra-grid');
      CARCASSES.forEach((c) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = 'cell';
        b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', 'false');
        b.dataset.id = c.id;
        b.innerHTML = `${c.emoji} ${c.name.replace(/, according to Rabbi Shimon/, ' (R. Shimon)')} <span class="!text-[#a39a8a]">in the ${c.where === 'village' ? 'villages' : 'markets'}: ${c.ans === 'intent' ? 'needs intent' : 'food'}</span>`;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          if (b.disabled) return;
          b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', b.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true' ? 'false' : 'true');
        });
        g.appendChild(b);
      });
    }
    $('contra-check').addEventListener('click', () => {
      let perfect = true;
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('#contra-grid .cell').forEach((b) => {
        const c = CARCASSES.find((x) => x.id === b.dataset.id)!;
        const should = c.ans === 'intent';
        const picked = b.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true';
        if (should !== picked) perfect = false;
        b.classList.add(should ? 'ok' : picked ? 'bad' : 'x');
        b.disabled = true;
      });
      ($('contra-check') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      score.contra = perfect ? 1 : 0;
      const fb = $('contra-fb');
      fb.classList.remove('hidden');
      fb.innerHTML = `<p><strong class="${perfect ? '!text-[#7fa88a]' : '!text-[#e0876a]'}">${perfect ? 'Exactly those four.' : 'The four outlined in green are the problem.'}</strong>
        Every ruling that still requires intent contradicts the theory, since each of those carcasses is already forbidden. <span dir="rtl" lang="he">״וְאִי אָמְרַתְּ אִיסּוּרוֹ חִישּׁוּבוֹ, לְמָה לִי מַחְשָׁבָה?״</span></p>
        <p class="mt-2">First the Gemara says this mishna is Rabbi Shimon's, and he rejects the theory. But the pig clause at the end is explicitly Rabbi Shimon's, so the unattributed opening can't be. And Rabbi Shimon's reason there is kosher signs, not prohibition. ${link('Bekhorot 10a:11')}</p>
        <p class="mt-2">So Rava concludes: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">״דְּכוּלֵּי עָלְמָא לָא אָמְרִינַן אִיסּוּרוֹ חִישּׁוּבוֹ״</span>. Nobody holds that a food's prohibition counts as its intent. ${link('Bekhorot 10a:12')}</p>`;
      $('crow').classList.remove('hidden');
      renderCrow(0);
    });

    const CROW = [
      `Rabbi Eliezer's point is that the prohibition on eating a crow counts as intent (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">אִיסּוּרוֹ חִישּׁוּבוֹ</span>), so the crow itself is food. Nimos agrees its blood makes other food susceptible, but thinks nobody meant to eat the crow, so the crow itself isn't food. The Rabbis and Rabbi Shimon would then have the same argument about a firstborn donkey slaughtered for practice. ${link('Bekhorot 10b:5')}`,
      `Perhaps a crow is different: it has <em>some</em> signs of a kosher bird, the same reason Rabbi Shimon gave for the pig. A donkey has none. Then why would they argue specifically about slaughtering <em>for practice</em>? Because of Nimos: even when the crow is slaughtered deliberately, he says practice slaughter doesn't make it food. Rabbi Eliezer would call it food even if it were killed carelessly. ${link('Bekhorot 10b:8')}`,
    ];
    function renderCrow(i: number) {
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-crow]').forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(Number(b.dataset.crow) === i)));
      $('crow-text').innerHTML = CROW[i];
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-crow]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => renderCrow(Number(b.dataset.crow))));

    // =============== PART II: the timeline ===============
    type V = 'P' | 'F';
    const LENSES = ['Rabbi Yehuda', 'Rabbi Shimon, per Rabba, Rav Naḥman and Reish Lakish', 'Rabbi Shimon, per Rabbi Yoḥanan'];
    const STOPS: { title: string; sub: string; ans: V[]; why: string; ref: string }[] = [
      {
        title: 'Alive and unredeemed: may he sell it or rent it out?',
        sub: 'Benefit from its value (the first clause of the baraita, as the Gemara finally reads it).',
        ans: ['F', 'P', 'P'],
        why: 'The Gemara reads the first clause as the living donkey\'s <em>value</em>: selling or renting. Rabbi Yehuda forbids it; Rabbi Shimon permits it. The dispute over after death is a separate question.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:13',
      },
      {
        title: 'Alive and unredeemed: may he shear it or work it?',
        sub: 'Benefit from its body (the later clause).',
        ans: ['F', 'P', 'P'],
        why: 'Same split. Both clauses are needed: otherwise you might think Rabbi Shimon concedes on the body itself, or Rabbi Yehuda concedes on its value.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:14',
      },
      {
        title: 'He gave the kohen a lamb: may he use the donkey now?',
        sub: 'Redemption.',
        ans: ['P', 'P', 'P'],
        why: 'Redemption is exactly what permits the donkey. That\'s why Safra thought "break its neck" might have worked like a redemption and needed a verse to say it doesn\'t.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:18',
      },
      {
        title: 'Neck broken: may he benefit from the carcass?',
        sub: 'The owner refused to redeem it.',
        ans: ['F', 'F', 'P'],
        why: 'Rabbi Yehuda forbids it, as he did while it was alive. Rabba, Rav Naḥman (citing Rabba bar Avuh) and Reish Lakish say Rabbi Shimon concedes after the neck is broken. Rabbi Yoḥanan, or Rabbi Elazar, says the dispute continues and Rabbi Shimon still permits it.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:24',
      },
    ];
    const lifeState: (V | null)[][] = STOPS.map(() => [null, null, null]);
    const lifeDone: boolean[] = STOPS.map(() => false);
    let lifeRight = 0;
    let toolOk = false;
    const range = $('life') as HTMLInputElement;

    function drawDonkey(stop: number) {
      const dead = stop === 3;
      const redeemed = stop === 2;
      const donkey = dead
        ? `<g fill="#6b6964"><ellipse cx="150" cy="84" rx="40" ry="11"/><path d="M188 82 L214 90 L212 97 L186 92 Z"/><rect x="118" y="92" width="26" height="4"/><rect x="152" y="93" width="26" height="4"/></g>
           <path d="M188 70 L198 84" stroke="#b4553a" stroke-width="3"/>`
        : `<g fill="#8c8a86"><ellipse cx="150" cy="62" rx="40" ry="17"/><rect x="120" y="72" width="7" height="26"/><rect x="170" y="72" width="7" height="26"/>
           <path d="M184 54 L208 30 L220 36 L198 62 Z"/><path d="M208 30 L204 12 L213 28 Z M214 32 L218 14 L221 32 Z"/><path d="M110 58 Q98 66 102 78" stroke="#8c8a86" stroke-width="4" fill="none"/></g>
           ${stop === 1 ? '<path d="M110 44 Q150 30 190 44" stroke="#efe8da" stroke-width="5" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="3 4"/>' : ''}`;
      const coin = stop === 0 ? '<circle cx="260" cy="40" r="14" fill="#d8b25a"/><text x="260" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14" fill="#1d1a17">₪</text><text x="260" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a8a">sale or rent</text>' : '';
      const wool = stop === 1 ? '<text x="260" y="72" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a8a">shearing, plowing</text>' : '';
      const lamb = redeemed
        ? '<g fill="#efe8da"><ellipse cx="262" cy="66" rx="20" ry="12"/><circle cx="283" cy="58" r="7"/></g><rect x="248" y="76" width="3" height="20" fill="#a39a8a"/><rect x="272" y="76" width="3" height="20" fill="#a39a8a"/><text x="262" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a8a">to the kohen</text>'
        : '';
      const cleaver = dead && toolOk ? '<path d="M226 38 L256 38 L256 54 L232 54 Z" fill="#b9c4c9"/><rect x="256" y="42" width="30" height="7" rx="2" fill="#6b4f35"/>' : '';
      $('life-svg').innerHTML = `<line x1="10" y1="99" x2="310" y2="99" stroke="#4a4235" stroke-width="2"/>${donkey}${coin}${wool}${lamb}${cleaver}`;
    }

    const TOOLS = [
      { t: 'A reed', ok: false },
      { t: 'A sickle', ok: false },
      { t: 'An ax', ok: false },
      { t: 'A saw', ok: false },
      { t: 'Lock it in a room to starve', ok: false },
      { t: 'A cleaver, from behind the neck', ok: true },
    ];
    let toolTries = 0;
    function renderTools() {
      const rack = $('tool-rack');
      rack.innerHTML = '';
      TOOLS.forEach((tool) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = 'act';
        b.textContent = tool.t;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          toolTries++;
          if (tool.ok) {
            toolOk = true;
            b.classList.add('ok');
            rack.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => ((x as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true));
            $('tool-fb').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#7fa88a]">"He breaks its neck with a cleaver from behind and buries it."</span> The reed, sickle, ax, saw and locked room are all ruled out. ${link('Bekhorot 10b:12')}`;
            renderStop();
          } else {
            b.classList.add('bad');
            b.disabled = true;
            $('tool-fb').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#e0876a]">The baraita rules that one out: "he may not kill it with a reed, a sickle, an ax or a saw, nor lock it in a room so it dies."</span>`;
          }
        });
        rack.appendChild(b);
      });
    }

    function renderStop() {
      const i = Number(range.value);
      const s = STOPS[i];
      drawDonkey(i);
      $('life-cap').textContent = s.title;
      $('life-sub').textContent = s.sub;
      const needTool = i === 3 && !toolOk;
      $('tools').classList.toggle('hidden', i !== 3);
      const lenses = $('lenses');
      lenses.innerHTML = '';
      lenses.classList.toggle('hidden', needTool);
      ($('life-check') as HTMLButtonElement).classList.toggle('hidden', needTool || lifeDone[i]);
      LENSES.forEach((name, li) => {
        const row = document.createElement('div');
        row.className = 'lens-row';
        const v = lifeState[i][li];
        const btn = document.createElement('button');
        btn.className = 'act verdict';
        if (v) btn.dataset.v = v;
        btn.textContent = v === 'P' ? 'Permitted' : v === 'F' ? 'Forbidden' : 'Tap to rule';
        btn.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name}: ${btn.textContent}`);
        if (lifeDone[i]) {
          btn.disabled = true;
          btn.classList.add(v === s.ans[li] ? 'ok' : 'bad');
          if (v !== s.ans[li]) btn.textContent += ` (${s.ans[li] === 'P' ? 'permitted' : 'forbidden'})`;
        }
        btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
          lifeState[i][li] = lifeState[i][li] === 'P' ? 'F' : 'P';
          renderStop();
          (lenses.querySelectorAll('button')[li] as HTMLButtonElement).focus();
        });
        row.innerHTML = `<span class="text-base">${name}</span>`;
        row.appendChild(btn);
        lenses.appendChild(row);
      });
      const fb = $('life-fb');
      if (lifeDone[i]) {
        fb.classList.remove('hidden');
        fb.innerHTML = `${s.why} ${link(s.ref)}`;
      } else fb.classList.add('hidden');
    }
    range.addEventListener('input', renderStop);
    $('life-check').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const i = Number(range.value);
      if (lifeState[i].some((v) => v === null)) {
        const fb = $('life-fb');
        fb.classList.remove('hidden');
        fb.textContent = 'Rule for all three before locking in.';
        return;
      }
      lifeDone[i] = true;
      lifeRight += lifeState[i].filter((v, li) => v === STOPS[i].ans[li]).length;
      renderStop();
      if (lifeDone.every(Boolean)) {
        score.life = lifeRight;
        $('proofs').classList.remove('hidden');
        renderProofs();
      } else {
        const nxt = lifeDone.findIndex((d) => !d);
        const fb = $('life-fb');
        fb.innerHTML += ` <span class="!text-[#a39a8a]">Next: drag to stop ${nxt + 1}.</span>`;
      }
    });

    const PROOFS = [
      {
        src: '"And if you do not redeem it, you shall break its neck" (Exodus 13:13). Breaking the neck is said here and of the heifer (Deuteronomy 21:4): just as the heifer is forbidden, so is the donkey.',
        rn: 'Rabbi Yehuda already forbids the living donkey, so why would he need a verse for the dead one? It must be Rabbi Shimon.',
        deflect: 'Safra\'s answer, via Rav Sheshet: it <em>is</em> Rabbi Yehuda. The verse sets breaking the neck in place of redemption, so you might think it permits the donkey the way redemption does. The gezera shava says it doesn\'t.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:18',
      },
      {
        src: 'Levi\'s baraita: why break its neck? "He caused the kohen a monetary loss, so his own money shall be lost."',
        rn: 'Under Rabbi Yehuda the donkey is already worthless to him. Only if Rabbi Shimon forbids the carcass does its value get lost here.',
        deflect: 'Either tanna works. Under Rabbi Yehuda, he loses the gap between the living donkey and the cheaper lamb he would have paid. Under Rabbi Shimon, even with the carcass permitted, a dead donkey is worth less than a live one.',
        ref: 'Bekhorot 10b:22',
      },
    ];
    let proofRight = 0;
    let proofsAnswered = 0;
    function renderProofs() {
      const list = $('proof-list');
      PROOFS.forEach((p) => {
        const d = document.createElement('div');
        d.className = 'rounded-lg border border-[#3a342b] p-4';
        d.innerHTML = `<p class="text-base">${p.src}</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]">Rav Naḥman: ${p.rn}</p>
          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button class="act" data-a="rs">Only Rabbi Shimon fits</button><button class="act" data-a="ry">Rabbi Yehuda could be the tanna</button></div>
          <p class="fb mt-3 hidden text-base leading-relaxed"></p>`;
        d.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach((b) =>
          b.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const ok = b.dataset.a === 'ry';
            if (ok) proofRight++;
            proofsAnswered++;
            d.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach((x) => {
              x.disabled = true;
              if (x.dataset.a === 'ry') x.classList.add('ok');
            });
            if (!ok) b.classList.add('bad');
            const fb = d.querySelector('.fb')!;
            fb.classList.remove('hidden');
            fb.innerHTML = `${p.deflect} ${link(p.ref)}`;
            if (proofsAnswered === PROOFS.length) {
              score.proofs = proofRight;
              checkFinale();
            }
          }),
        );
        list.appendChild(d);
      });
    }

    // =============== PART III: the scale ===============
    type Lens = 'rs' | 'ry-any' | 'ry-shekel';
    let lens: Lens = 'rs';
    let won = false;
    const dv = $('donkey-val') as HTMLInputElement;
    const fmt = (q: number) => {
      const whole = Math.floor(q / 4);
      const frac = ['', '¼', '½', '¾'][q % 4];
      if (!whole) return `${frac} shekel`;
      return `${whole}${frac} shekel${whole > 1 || frac ? 's' : ''}`;
    };
    function renderScale() {
      const q = Number(dv.value); // quarter-shekels
      $('donkey-val-out').textContent = fmt(q);
      let lamb = 0;
      let her = 0;
      let lambLabel = '';
      if (lens === 'rs') {
        her = q;
        lambLabel = 'no lamb needed';
      } else if (lens === 'ry-any') {
        lamb = 0.2;
        her = q - lamb;
        lambLabel = 'a lamb worth almost nothing';
      } else {
        lamb = 4;
        her = Math.max(0, q - 4);
        lambLabel = 'a lamb worth a shekel';
      }
      const tilt = Math.max(-14, Math.min(14, (q - lamb) * 2.2));
      const lambR = lens === 'rs' ? 0 : lens === 'ry-any' ? 6 : 12;
      const coins = Array.from({ length: Math.min(12, Math.ceil(her)) }, (_, k) => `<circle cx="${236 + (k % 6) * 12}" cy="${158 - Math.floor(k / 6) * 10}" r="5" fill="#d8b25a"/>`).join('');
      $('scale').innerHTML = `
        <rect x="156" y="40" width="8" height="118" fill="#5a5143"/><rect x="120" y="156" width="80" height="6" fill="#5a5143"/>
        <g id="beam" style="transform-origin:160px 40px; transform: rotate(${-tilt}deg)">
          <rect x="40" y="37" width="240" height="6" rx="3" fill="#b9c4c9"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="40" x2="60" y2="80" stroke="#7a7264"/><line x1="260" y1="40" x2="260" y2="80" stroke="#7a7264"/>
          <path d="M30 80 L90 80 L80 90 L40 90 Z" fill="#7a7264"/><path d="M230 80 L290 80 L280 90 L240 90 Z" fill="#7a7264"/>
          <g fill="#8c8a86"><ellipse cx="60" cy="${70 - Math.min(10, q)}" rx="${10 + q}" ry="${5 + q / 3}"/></g>
          ${lambR ? `<ellipse cx="260" cy="${76 - lambR / 2}" rx="${lambR + 4}" ry="${lambR / 1.6 + 2}" fill="#efe8da"/>` : ''}
        </g>
        <text x="60" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a8a">the donkey</text>
        <text x="260" y="118" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#a39a8a">${lambLabel}</text>
        <text x="264" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#d8b25a">in her hand</text>${coins}`;
      const betrothed = her > 0;
      $('scale-read').innerHTML = betrothed
        ? `She receives <strong>${lens === 'ry-any' ? 'just under ' + fmt(q) : fmt(her)}</strong>, so she <strong class="!text-[#e0876a]">is</strong> betrothed. That contradicts the mishna.`
        : `She receives <strong>nothing</strong>: the lamb swallows the whole value. She is <strong class="!text-[#7fa88a]">not</strong> betrothed, matching the mishna.`;
      if (!betrothed && !won) {
        won = true;
        score.scale = 1;
        const w = $('scale-win');
        w.classList.remove('hidden');
        w.innerHTML = `That's Rav's case, via Rabba bar Avuh: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">״לְעוֹלָם רַבִּי יְהוּדָה, וּכְגוֹן שֶׁאֵינוֹ שָׁוֶה אֶלָּא שֶׁקֶל״</span>. Rabbi Yehuda, a donkey worth only a shekel, and Rabbi Yosei bar Yehuda's rule that no redemption is less than a shekel. Under the Rabbis' "any amount" the lamb can always cost less than the donkey, so something is left over for her. ${link('Bekhorot 10b:27')}
          <span class="mt-2 block text-sm !text-[#a39a8a]">The other version (Rav Naḥman): the mishna means after the neck is broken, when everyone, Rabbi Shimon included, forbids benefit. ${link('Bekhorot 10b:25')}</span>`;
        $('verse').classList.remove('hidden');
        renderVerse();
      }
    }
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lens]').forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        lens = b.dataset.lens as Lens;
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lens]').forEach((x) => x.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(x === b)));
        renderScale();
      }),
    );
    dv.addEventListener('input', renderScale);

    const VERSES = [
      { t: '"From a month old you shall redeem them… five shekels of silver" (Numbers 18:16)', ok: false, fb: 'That\'s the comparison to a firstborn son, which would demand five and thirty days. The baraita\'s doubled <em>tifdeh</em> rejects it.' },
      { t: '"All your valuations shall be with the shekel of the Sanctuary" (Leviticus 27:25)', ok: true, fb: 'Rava: <span dir="rtl" lang="he">״כׇּל עֲרָכִין שֶׁאַתָּה מַעֲרִיךְ לֹא יְהוּ פְּחוּתִין מִשֶּׁקֶל״</span>. Any valuation you assess is at least a shekel. No comparison to the firstborn son needed.' },
      { t: '"And if you do not redeem it, you shall break its neck" (Exodus 13:13)', ok: false, fb: 'That verse is about what happens without redemption. It says nothing about the lamb\'s price.' },
    ];
    function renderVerse() {
      const box = $('verse-choices');
      box.innerHTML = '';
      VERSES.forEach((v) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.className = 'act text-left';
        b.textContent = v.t;
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          box.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x, k) => {
            (x as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
            if (VERSES[k].ok) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (!v.ok) b.classList.add('bad');
          score.verse = v.ok ? 1 : 0;
          const fb = $('verse-fb');
          fb.classList.remove('hidden');
          fb.innerHTML = `${v.fb} ${link('Bekhorot 10b:32')}`;
          checkFinale();
        });
        box.appendChild(b);
      });
    }

    // =============== finale ===============
    function checkFinale() {
      if (Object.values(score).some((v) => v === undefined)) return;
      const total = Object.values(score).reduce((a, b) => (a ?? 0) + (b ?? 0), 0) as number;
      const max = Object.values(MAX).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
      $('finale').classList.remove('hidden');
      $('finale-text').textContent = `${total}/${max} rulings right. The donkey is buried; the lamb, if there ever was one, is with the kohen.`;
    }

    renderSort();
    renderTools();
    renderStop();
    renderScale();
  </script>
</Layout>
